{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, sorry you're stuck on day one. Your account is active and isn't locked. It's just waiting for you to set your own password. Your three tries didn't lock you out. Most of the time this error means the new password doesn't meet our rules, so please try again like this:\n\n1. Use the Windows sign-in screen on your Brightline laptop, not a web page. Make sure you're plugged into the office network or connected to VPN.\n2. Type your temporary password. Watch for Caps Lock, the keyboard language, and characters that look alike (l vs I, 0 vs O).\n3. Pick a new password that's at least 14 characters long and that you haven't used recently. A short phrase works well, for example several words together.\n\nIf it still fails, please reply and tell us: (a) were you on the laptop sign-in screen or a web page, (b) were you in the office, at home on VPN, or at home without VPN, and (c) the exact wording of the error. Please don't include any passwords in your reply. If we need to issue a new temporary password, we'll give it to you by phone.",
  "internal_note": "Followed KB-003. lookup_user (id 12): status active, must_change_password=true, failed_login_count=0, not blocked, VPN access on, device BL-LT-0112. password_last_set 2026-10-09 (the temp password). Sign-in logs: 9 successful sign-ins, all from New York on the corporate network or her usual residential VPN during work hours. No failures, nothing suspicious. The account isn't locked, so no unlock needed. The most likely causes are a new password that breaks policy (under 14 characters or reused) or trying the change on a web page or off-network. I sent her the KB-003 steps and asked where she's attempting the change, which network she's on, and the exact error text. Next steps if it still fails: if she gets locked out, unlock (KB-001). If the temp password itself is rejected, issue a new one per KB-002, delivered by phone. If the account shows active with no change required and still no password works, escalate to Tier 2.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-003"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
